            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Bob obtains $3>x-2$, so $x<5$. For the correct solution, $x\\ne2$. Multiply by $(x-2)^2>0$: $$\\begin{align*}3(x-2)&>(x-2)^2\\\\(x-2)^2-3(x-2)&<0\\\\(x-2)(x-5)&<0.\\end{align*}$$ The product is negative between its roots, so $2<x<5$. Bob's result contains this interval but also includes $x<2$, where multiplying by $x-2$ reverses the inequality, and $x=2$, where the expression is undefined.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
